{"name":"Chicago Skyline","hex":"#96adba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"skyline","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The line that seems to be the boundary of the sky and the ground; the horizon.","The horizontal silhouette of a city or building against the sky."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To outline something against the sky.","To filter by means of the skyline operator."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skyline"}],"entries":[{"title":"Architecture of Chicago","blocks":[{"text":"The buildings and architecture of Chicago reflect the city's history and multicultural heritage, featuring prominent buildings in a variety of styles. Most structures downtown were destroyed by the Great Chicago Fire in 1871."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Chicago_Sears_Tower.jpg/330px-Chicago_Sears_Tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Architecture_of_Chicago"},{"title":"Chicago","blocks":[{"text":"Chicago is the most populous city in the U.S. state of Illinois and in the Midwestern United States. Located on the western shore of Lake Michigan, it is the third-most populous city in the United States and the fifth-most populous city in North America, with a population of 2.74 million at the 2020 census. The Chicago metropolitan area has approximately 9.62 million residents according to the 2020 census and is the third-largest metropolitan statistical area in the country and part of the fourth-largest combined statistical area in the United States, spanning 19 counties in three states and with a population of nearly 10 million. Chicago is the county seat of Cook County, the second-most populous county in the U.S."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg/330px-Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicago"},{"title":"Skyline","blocks":[{"text":"A skyline is the outline or shape viewed near the horizon. It can be created by a city's overall structure, or by human intervention in a rural setting, or in nature that is formed where the sky meets buildings or the land."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Lower_Manhattan_from_Governors_Island_with_a_fishing_boat_%2846294p%29.jpg/330px-Lower_Manhattan_from_Governors_Island_with_a_fishing_boat_%2846294p%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skyline"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/2010-02-19_16500x2000_chicago_skyline_panorama.jpg/500px-2010-02-19_16500x2000_chicago_skyline_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/2010-02-19_16500x2000_chicago_skyline_panorama.jpg/1280px-2010-02-19_16500x2000_chicago_skyline_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/2010-02-19_16500x2000_chicago_skyline_panorama.jpg/500px-2010-02-19_16500x2000_chicago_skyline_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The 2010 Chicago skyline as seen from the Adler Planetarium (use cursor to identify buildings)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2010-02-19_16500x2000_chicago_skyline_panorama.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/2004-06-09_1200x1600_chicago_chicago_building.jpg/500px-2004-06-09_1200x1600_chicago_chicago_building.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/2004-06-09_1200x1600_chicago_chicago_building.jpg/500px-2004-06-09_1200x1600_chicago_chicago_building.jpg?u